      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\) given that \\(AB\\) is a diameter of the circle, and \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\).\n\nFirst, let's analyze the given information and the properties of the circle and tangents:\n1. \\(AB\\) is a diameter of the circle, so \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle AEB = \\angle AOB = 90^\\circ\\).\n2. The tangents at \\(B\\) and \\(E\\) are perpendicular to the radii \\(OB\\) and \\(OE\\) respectively. This means that \\(\\angle OBE = \\angle OEB = 90^\\circ\\).\n3. \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\). Since \\(\\angle BAE\\) and \\(\\angle OAE\\) are supplementary angles (they form a straight line), we have \\(\\angle OAE = 180^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 137^\\circ\\).\n\nNext, we need to find \\(\\angle CED\\). Note that \\(\\angle CED\\) is an angle formed by the intersection of the tangents at \\(B\\) and \\(E\\) with the chord \\(AE\\). The angle between two tangents from a point to a circle is given by \\(2\\angle EOA\\), where \\(O\\) is the center of the circle and \\(E\\) is the point of tangency on \\(AE\\).\n\nSince \\(\\angle EOA = 180^\\circ - \\angle AOE\\), we have \\(\\angle EOA = 180^\\circ - 137^\\circ = 43^\\circ\\). Therefore, \\(\\angle CED = 2 \\times 43^\\circ = 86^\\circ\\).\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\) is \\(\\boxed{86}\\).",
