      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\) given the geometric relationships and conditions provided. Let's proceed step by step.\n\n1. **Identify Given Information and Relationships:**\n   - \\(AB\\) is a diameter of the circle centered at \\(O\\).\n   - \\(E\\) is a point on the circle.\n   - \\(B\\) and \\(E\\) are points of tangency.\n   - \\(C\\) is the intersection of the tangent at \\(B\\) and the tangent at \\(E\\).\n   - \\(D\\) is the intersection of \\(AE\\) and \\(BC\\).\n   - \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Analyze the Tangent Properties:**\n   - Since \\(B\\) and \\(E\\) are points of tangency, the tangents from a point outside the circle to the points of tangency are equal in length.\n   - The tangent at \\(B\\) is perpendicular to the radius \\(OB\\).\n   - The tangent at \\(E\\) is perpendicular to the radius \\(OE\\).\n\n3. **Use the Intersecting Chords Theorem:**\n   - The intersecting chords theorem states that the product of the lengths of the segments of one chord is equal to the product of the lengths of the segments of the other chord.\n   - In this case, \\(AB\\) is a diameter, so \\(AB\\) is the hypotenuse of the right triangle \\(AOB\\).\n\n4. **Relate Angles:**\n   - Since \\(AB\\) is the diameter, \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\).\n   - \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\), so \\(\\angle ABE = 47^\\circ\\) (since \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle ABE\\) and \\(\\angle EAB\\) are complementary).\n\n5. **Determine \\(\\angle CED\\):**\n   - Notice that \\(\\angle CED\\) is an angle subtended by the same arc \\(CE\\) in the circle.\n   - Since \\(E\\) is on the circle, \\(\\angle CED\\) is an angle in the same segment as \\(\\angle AEB\\).\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle CED = \\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\).\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\) is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
